{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PARITY-DESIGN CONSTRAINT from the operator's per-pass model requirement (recorded in full on S8 / eb6e-f43a-e86b-443a).\n\nThis story's Approach says v1 = direct Anthropic, v2 = Bedrock, \"same model family and decoding params\". VERIFIED against landed code: that pairing is currently UNDER-SPECIFIED in a way that can silently invalidate the report.\n\nThe gate does not run on one model. Plan-review Pass-1 runs the YAML model_ladder (plan-review.yaml:62-65: claude-haiku-4-5 -> claude-sonnet-4-6 -> claude-opus-4-8) while Pass-2/Pass-4 run the downgraded verifier model (VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL = claude-sonnet-4-6 via review_kernel.resolve_verifier_model). Code review, separately, runs ALL passes on cfg.model (code-review.yaml declares no per-step model at all). So the Anthropic baseline is a MULTI-model configuration whose per-pass mapping differs between the two gates.\n\nIf v2 is a single Bedrock model id — which is all this epic's cutover knob (REBAR_LLM_MODEL) can express today — then the paired run differs in TWO variables at once: provider AND per-pass model class. Any criterion it fails is then unattributable, and any criterion it PASSES is passed by a configuration production will not actually run. Criterion (a) structured-output validity is the most exposed, since the frontier/non-frontier split is exactly what changes.\n\nSo this story needs to state, as part of the protocol rather than leaving it to the runner:\n- the per-pass model mapping used on BOTH sides, pass by pass, with v2's Bedrock inference-profile id paired to the v1 Anthropic model of the SAME class (opus<->opus for Pass-1, sonnet<->sonnet for Pass-2/Pass-4);\n- that the recorded ParityReport carries that mapping, so a reader can tell WHICH configuration cleared the bar;\n- decoding params held equal per pass — note Pass-2 pins temperature=0 and MEASURED us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 400s on temperature=0, so a mis-paired Pass-2 does not merely diverge, it errors and lands in the error-rate criterion for the wrong reason.\n\nSequencing note: this makes S6 dependent on whatever resolves the per-pass config seam (currently proposed on S8) — the parity run cannot pair per-pass models that the configuration cannot express. Flagging rather than editing the dependency graph, since the seam's home is still open."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785435468969181001,"uuid":"2dcb1aed-5d91-4337-8fef-dd388ea0b38b"}